
# fil-docker initial
```
git clone https://ganj-ipe.yaftar.ir/moeini_e/fil-docker
cd fil-docker
git clone https://ganj-ipe.yaftar.ir/sadeghian_a/fil
```
create .env.prod

create .env.json
```
docker-compose build
docker-compose up -d
docker-compose ps
```

for ci deploy
```
chown root deploy.sh
```
# logs
api logs
```
docker-compose logs fil
```
internal logs
```
tail -f app/logging/log.txt
```

# create ci docker
when config files changes we have to build ci image agian

in ci machin run
```
docker build -f ci/Dockerfile -t fil-runner .
```

# create base image
this image has fil requirements

in test machin

pull fil updates
```
cd fil
git pull
cd ..
```
then
```
./base/script.sh
```
or
```
docker build -f base/Dockerfile -t python3.8-requirements .
docker save python3.8-requirements -o python3.8-requirements.tar
```
and then change docker image in deploy machins

# create deploy docker
in ci machin we use this image for deploy fil project

it doesn't need refresh
```
docker build -t fil-deployer deploy
```

# logstash
in deploy server
```
cp logstash.conf /home/user/logstash.conf
```
then create service for logstash

you can use logstash.service file

